    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The view that biology is the sole determining factor and everything else is merely social construction is not the currently dominant scientific position; rather, it is considered an oversimplification. Modern biology acknowledges that while genes and hormones are foundational, factors like brain development and hormonal fluctuations create a spectrum of human experience. Therefore, the scientific community largely views this rigid dichotomy as an incomplete model rather than an actively debated scientific disagreement at this level.",
      "source": "target",
